You take the backpack off your back, and sink slowly on the ground, right on the soft underlayer of grass. You can hardly keep your eyes open, your mind is clouded...
"Hey, Henry, what is wrong with you?" you hear a worried voice of Conan.
"Nothing ...eh...Conan, let's have rest for a little. Maybe take a nap?"
"What are you talking about?! Listen, you're so pale! Henry!.."
Everything is swimming before your eyes. As if you are looking from aside you see Conan pull your arm, trying to pick up Doyle, who is lying next to you. Then you lapse into deep oblivion.
When you recover consciousness, you find yourself in the shade with no sick fragrance to be scented. You slowly open your eyes. It seems to be the very underbrush you wanted to reach. You sit, leaning your back against the tree; Doyle still unconscious is not far. Conan is sitting near, watching at you intently.
"I thought you'd never..." he exhaled with relief.
"What happened to me?"
"Maybe it`s all those damn plants. Even I got a headache, pulling you two out of there. You just went all weak at the knees and fell with no response."
"Thanks buddy..."
You hardly stand up. After awhile, Doyle opens his eyes with a low groan.